  i This slice() call subtracts from .length to count from the end.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ (foo as string[]).slice((foo as string[]).length - 1);
      │                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ (array as number[]).splice((array as number[]).length - 2, 1);
    4 │ Array.prototype.slice.call(foo as any[], (foo as any[]).length - 1);
  
  i slice() accepts negative indexes, which count back from the end, so the subtraction makes the position harder to read.
  
  i Use a negative index instead, such as -1 for array.length - 1.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use a negative index.
  
    2 │ (foo·as·string[]).slice((foo·as·string[]).length·-·1);
      │                         ------------------------- -   

